# Run with NFSU2_PAD=hotplug, the synthetic pad plugged in (PLUG=1).  Pad
# front end: View opens the quit prompt (the posted 'q'), B cancels it; the
# left stick moves through the menus (POV 1) to Options > Controls > Joypad
# Configuration.  Unplugged there, the pad stays on the page (no
# DIERR_INPUTLOST) and editing one of its bindings with the keyboard does not
# crash (the game reads its object list from when the page opened); plugged
# back in, it binds again; once the page is left it is lost (hotplug) and
# found again by the game's rescan.
0:untilpad:START:MC_Background.fng:120
+200:padtap:A
+0:wait:GarageMain.fng:3000
+600:padtap:BACK
+200:shot
+5:padtap:B
+200:shot
+5:pad:LX=1
+20:pad:LX=0
+40:pad:LX=1
+20:pad:LX=0
+40:pad:LX=1
+20:pad:LX=0
+40:pad:LX=1
+20:pad:LX=0
+40:pad:LX=1
+20:pad:LX=0
+100:padtap:A
+0:wait:UI_OptionsMain.fng:600
+300:pad:LX=1
+20:pad:LX=0
+100:pad:LX=1
+20:pad:LX=0
+100:pad:LX=1
+20:pad:LX=0
+100:pad:LX=1
+20:pad:LX=0
+100:padtap:A
+0:wait:UI_Options_PC_Controller.fng:600
+300:pad:LY=-1
+20:pad:LY=0
+100:pad:LX=1
+20:pad:LX=0
+200:padtap:DDOWN
+40:padtap:DDOWN
+60:log:unplug on the Joypad page
+0:pad:PLUG=0
+120:DOWN
+60:DOWN
+60:log:edit a binding of the unplugged pad with the keyboard
+0:RETURN
+200:shot
+5:ESCAPE
+200:log:plug it back in
+0:pad:PLUG=1
+150:padtap:DDOWN
+60:padtap:A
+200:padtap:Y
+200:shot
+5:padtap:B
+200:padtap:B
+300:log:left the Controls page: unplug, then plug back in
+0:pad:PLUG=0
+120:pad:PLUG=1
+200:log:end
